  "inherits": "obdumper-4.3.5-slice-v5.json",
  "revisionReason": "EX-I3 verified subset: promotes the eight CSV serialization parameters to ENABLED and adds CSV options (with-trim), compression (compress/compression-algo), file layout (no-nested-dir/max-file-size/retain-empty-files), filtering (query-sql/include-exclude-column-names/exclude-virtual-columns/flashback-scn/flashback-timestamp) and resource (thread/page-size/parallel-macro/fetch-size/mem) parameters. EX-I4 verified subset: adds CUT (--cut/--trail-delimiter/--remove-newline) and SQL (--sql) data formats, extends shared text serialization parameters (escape-character/null-string/with-trim to CSV+CUT; line-separator/file-encoding to CSV+CUT+SQL) and compression parameters to the new formats. EX-I4 official re-check (V4.3.6 command-line options page, 2026-08-07): file layout, filtering and performance parameters carry no format restriction and officially combine with any data format option, so no-nested-dir/max-file-size/retain-empty-files/query-sql/include-exclude-column-names/exclude-virtual-columns/flashback-scn/flashback-timestamp/thread/page-size/parallel-macro/fetch-size/mem also bind to export-odp-cut-v1 and export-odp-sql-v1. EX-I4 POS validation (2026-08-07 controlled test on the actual 4.3.5 binary): POS is a standalone data format via --pos and MUST be combined with --ctl-path and a <table>.ctrl control file (position(byte-length) fixed-length columns); the official V4.3.6 'CUT plus empty column-splitter' wording does not match 4.3.5 behavior, so --pos/--ctl-path bind to the new export-odp-pos-v1 capability and --column-splitter stays CUT-only and is enabled for export-odp-cut-v1. Date-time value formats and compression-level stay VALIDATION_GATED until facts are verified. EX-I5 structured formats (2026-08-07): --par/--orc/--avro bind to export-odp-parquet-v1/export-odp-orc-v1/export-odp-avro-v1; official V4.3.6 format tables list file-encoding and flashback-scn for all three formats, flashback-timestamp applies to any data format, and filtering/performance/file-layout parameters carry no format restriction, so they bind to the structured capabilities as well; compression stays readable-format-only (CSV/CUT/POS/SQL) and --block-size is not bound (officially ineffective for ORC/Parquet; Avro unverified). All new parameters bind to export-odp-cut-v1 and export-odp-sql-v1; completeness is guaranteed by control-plane configuration validation. EX-I7 DDL behavior (2026-08-10): --drop-object and --retain-schema bind to export-odp-ddl-v1 and export-odp-ddl-csv-v1 and are emitted only for DDL content (DDL_ONLY/DDL_AND_DATA); --add-extra-message stays unbound until sys-credential availability is verified, --compact-schema/--sequence-policy stay VALIDATION_GATED until controlled facts are verified. EX-I7 block-size (2026-08-10): --block-size binds to the readable-format and full-CSV capabilities (full-csv/ddl-csv/cut/sql/pos) with MB/ROW explicit values verified on the actual 4.3.5 binary (2026-08-07); it stays unbound for PARQUET/ORC (officially ineffective) and AVRO (unverified), the default-value documentation conflict (0 vs 1024MB) remains a low-risk residual because the wizard emits the parameter only when explicitly set. EX-I7 compression-level (2026-08-10): --compression-level binds to the same readable-format capabilities and follows the official per-algorithm ranges (zstd 1-22 default 3, zlib -1-9 default -1; gzip/snappy do not support a level); the control plane fails closed when the level is carried without compression or with an unsupported algorithm. EX-I7 remaining parameters batch 1 (2026-08-11 controlled tests on the actual 4.3.5 binary): --compact-schema (DDL_ONLY, show create table retrieved text, byte-identical with baseline on the current schema) binds to the ddl/ddl-csv capabilities and is emitted only for DDL content; --where (row-filtering verified: 109 rows vs 1,000) conflicts with --query-sql per the official constraint; --snapshot (consistency snapshot) and --weak-read (follower read) are valueless switches verified on the actual binary; --retry (resume from last checkpoint) fails closed without a .dump.ckpt and its resume path moves to EX-I8. --partition/--exclude-data-types/--enable-hidden-pk and the timestamp value formats stay VALIDATION_GATED until the next controlled batch.",
